                    insight_vested:         `Vested partnership: you transformed a failing transactional deal into an aligned, outcome-based relationship. The gainshare made Apex profit from the savings it creates, the automation is unlocked, and the $7.7M holds on TCO — with lower service risk than a re-bid and governance that handles the unforeseen.`,
                    insight_squeeze:        `Squeeze backfired: you drove the rate down and hit the number on paper, but starved the automation and reignited the adversarial dynamic. Apex now bleeds margin on your account with even less reason to innovate — and next peak season the structural problem returns, worse.`,
                    insight_hollow:         `Vested in name only: you adopted the relational vocabulary and a values charter while leaving the pay-per-activity economics untouched, or split savings with no agreed baseline. Apex still loses revenue by helping you save — so it won't, and the “partnership” unravels into the same fee fights.`,
                    insight_short:          `You didn't fully cure the inverted incentive. The model, the economics and the negotiation still pull in slightly different directions — enough for the relationship to slide back toward the transactional default at the next shock.`,
                    insight_savings_short:  `You fell short of the CFO's $7.7M run-rate mandate. Without the unlocked automation savings — or with too much given away in the gainshare — the number doesn't close, and the re-bid threat regains the floor.`,
                    insight_savings_met:    `You delivered the CFO's $7.7M run-rate savings — and, crucially, did it through unlocked efficiency rather than a one-year rate squeeze, so the number is durable into year two and beyond.`,
                    insight_bluff:          `You over-played the re-bid. Apex could see the 9–12 month, $6–9M switching reality, so the bluff weakened rather than strengthened your hand. A re-bid is a credible floor, not a credible threat to use lightly.`,
                    insight_aligned:        `Alignment is high and risk low — Apex's economics now move with yours, the governance is relational, and the deal is built to absorb the contingency neither side wrote down. That is the disclosure of a relationship transformed, not just repriced.`,

                    hint_squeeze:           `You took the squeeze path. It books a one-year saving but deepens the misalignment — pivot toward outcome-based pricing and a gainshare so efficiency, not activity, is what Apex is paid for.`,
